    "wacc_rationale": "USD flows, USD rate. Risk-free ~4.3% (10y UST), ERP 5.0%, beta ~1.05 -> cost of equity ~9.5%; pre-tax cost of debt ~5.0% (A-rated) -> ~3.8% after tax; debt incl. finance and operating leases ~$19.2B vs ~$71.5B market cap (~21% debt weight) -> WACC ~8.3%, rounded to 8.5%. Same WACC in all three scenarios: risk is charged through the probability-weighted scenarios, not a WACC premium.",
    "lease_treatment": "US GAAP: operating-lease cost (~$691M FY2025) is straight-line rent inside SG&A/COGS, so it is already inside EBITDA and the flows; operating-lease liabilities ($3.3B non-current) are therefore NOT in net debt. Finance-lease liabilities (~$2.1B) are inside LongTermDebtAndCapitalLeaseObligations and their amortisation is inside D&A, so they sit in total_debt. One treatment, applied once.",
    "nci_treatment": "None - Target has no material non-controlling interests.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (US operating retailer; routing table row 1/2 - consumer, moderately cyclical). No prior TGT DCF and no MEMORY entry: fresh build. ANCHORS: net debt = $14,221M long-term debt and finance leases + $1,136M current portion - $5,411M cash at 2026-08-01 (Q2 FY2026 10-Q via SEC XBRL companyfacts; cash is mid-year and seasonally low-to-mid vs the January peak). FY0 EBITDA margin: GAAP EBITDA $8,251M (op income 5,117 + D&A 3,134) + SBC 282 = $8,533M = 8.1% of revenue, but FY2025 Q1 carried ~$593M of one-off interchange-litigation settlement gains, so the underlying pre-SBC margin was ~7.6%. TARIFF REFUND: the $994M pretax IEEPA tariff refund recognised in Q2 FY2026 is EXCLUDED from every projected margin (Y1 base 8.3% = guided ~6% op margin less the ~90bp refund, + D&A ~3.0%, + SBC). It is not added to the bridge either: whatever has been collected is already inside the 2026-08-01 cash; any uncollected receivable (~$755M after tax, ~$1.65/share) is unmodelled upside. WORKING CAPITAL: inventory $13.2B ~ payables $13.3B at 2026-08-01, so growth is close to cash-neutral; wc_capture 0 (bear -2). BUYBACKS: $408M FY2025, ~$3M H1 FY2026 - repurchases effectively paused while capex steps up to ~$5B, so the flat count is a modelling convention Target is currently funding only partly. Interest income not stripped: Target is net debt. Horizon 10 years because capex (~4.5% of revenue in FY2026) is well above its mature ~3.4-3.6% and the margin is still recovering in year 5. Engine discounts year 1 as a full year from the valuation date although H1 FY2026 is already complete - a small conservative approximation. Fiscal-year labels in Metrics.csv run one year ahead of Target's own naming (CSV FY2026 = Target fiscal 2025), and the XBRL quarter rows for FY2026 are labelled 'Q2 2027'/'Q3 2027' (= Target Q1/Q2 2026).",
